---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { getSupabaseClient } from '../lib/supabase';

const supabase = getSupabaseClient();
const { data: settings } = await supabase.from('site_settings').select('contact_email').single();
const contactEmail = settings?.contact_email ?? null;

const LAST_UPDATED = '23 September 2026';
---

<Layout title="Cookies — JTP Skulptur" description="What cookies and local storage JTP Skulptur's website actually uses.">
  <header class="mx-auto max-w-(--measure-full) px-4 pt-14 sm:px-8 sm:pt-20">
    <p class="caption">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="font-display mt-3 text-3xl sm:text-5xl">Cookies</h1>
  </header>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-(--measure-content) px-4 py-10 sm:px-8 sm:py-14">
    <p class="caption">Last updated {LAST_UPDATED}</p>

    <div class="mt-6 border-l-2 border-(--color-clay) pl-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-(--color-ink-soft)">
      <p>
        This page is a direct audit of what this website actually stores in your browser — not a generic template.
        It has not been legally reviewed; treat it as an accurate technical account rather than a finalised legal
        document.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">Our approach</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      JTP Skulptur's website uses the cookies and browser storage that are strictly necessary for it to work. With
      your consent only, it also uses Google Analytics 4 to measure, in aggregate, how the site is used. We do not
      use advertising or marketing cookies. Analytics is off by default: nothing is requested from Google until you
      press Accept in the cookie banner.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">Strictly necessary cookies</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      When a staff member or studio partner signs in to the password-protected admin or vendor area, we set one
      session cookie to keep them signed in. It is set only at that moment — ordinary visitors browsing, shopping,
      or subscribing to the newsletter never receive it. This cookie is essential (not optional): it can't be
      disabled without breaking sign-in, is not readable by any script, and is never used for tracking or
      advertising.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">Local storage (not a cookie)</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      Your shopping cart is kept in your browser's local storage, on your own device only. It stores the items and
      quantities you've added — nothing about you personally — and is never sent to our servers until you begin
      checkout. Clearing your browser's site data will empty your cart. Your cookie choice (Accept or Decline) is
      also remembered in local storage, so you aren't asked again on every page.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">Payment (Stripe)</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      When you check out, you're redirected to Stripe's own secure, hosted payment page. Any cookies set at that
      point belong to Stripe and are covered by
      {' '}<a href="https://stripe.com/cookies-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-(--color-clay) hover:underline">Stripe's own cookie policy</a>,
      not this website's.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">Analytics (Google Analytics 4) — only with your consent</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      If you press Accept, the site loads Google Analytics 4 and sets two analytics cookies on your device,
      <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_&lt;ID&gt;</code>, each lasting up to two years. They let us count visits and
      see, in aggregate, which pages are viewed, roughly where visitors come from, and which device and browser they
      use. We have switched off Google's advertising features and Google signals, and we remove sensitive parameters
      (such as a checkout session ID) from the page address before it is sent. If you press Decline — or don't
      choose — the Google Analytics script is never loaded and no analytics cookies are set.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      Analytics data that is tied to cookies or identifiers is kept for up to 14 months from a visitor's most recent
      visit, and detailed event-level data for 2 months. Aggregated statistics, which don't identify anyone, are
      kept longer.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      Google may process this data outside the European Economic Area.
      <strong class="text-(--color-clay)">[Confirm]</strong> the international-transfer safeguards that apply.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">Marketing</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      We do not use advertising or marketing cookies of any kind.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">Cookie consent</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      The first time you visit, a banner asks whether you accept analytics cookies. Accepting and declining are
      equally easy, and the rest of the site works the same either way. You can change your mind at any time using
      “Cookie settings” in the footer of every page — declining after previously accepting removes the analytics
      cookies from your browser. Strictly necessary cookies and local storage don't need consent under frameworks
      like the GDPR/ePrivacy rules. <strong class="text-(--color-clay)">[Confirm]</strong> this set-up against your
      applicable jurisdiction if you'd like additional assurance.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">Managing cookies &amp; local storage</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      Use “Cookie settings” in the footer to change your analytics choice at any time. You can also clear cookies
      and local storage for this site through your browser's settings. Doing so will sign you out of the admin or
      vendor area (if you were signed in), empty your shopping cart, and reset your cookie choice.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">More about your data</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      For how we handle the personal information you provide directly (contact form, newsletter, orders), see our
      {' '}<a href="/privacy" class="text-(--color-clay) hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">Contact</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      {contactEmail ? (
        <>Questions about this page can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`} class="text-(--color-clay) hover:underline">{contactEmail}</a>.</>
      ) : (
        <>Questions about this page can be sent via our <a href="/contact" class="text-(--color-clay) hover:underline">contact page</a>.</>
      )}
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
